          found by an outsider: glyphs (ours), predicate arity (Kimi K3,
          same day), bare ASCII terms (you). The script printed
          '✓ notation closed' before each one. 'Closed' had come to mean
          'closed with respect to whatever we happened to check'. That is
          the failure the checker exists to prevent, committed by the
          checker, three times. A term axis was built, measured at 271 hits
          (mostly prose), tightened to 37 (still mostly field accesses,
          enum members, ∃-bound names) — and NOT shipped as a gate. It is
          advisory-only. Regex cannot separate those classes; it should be
          rebuilt on our VSL parser. A 37-hit gate would be ignored within
          a week, and an ignored gate is worse than none.",
    },
    s2_channel: {
      verdict: "CORRECT. channels{} declared only φ↑/φ↓/ψ, so with A4
